 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>The <b>Font</b> class (in <code>java.awt</code>) is used to draw text in a special typeface, style and size.</p><h3>Key points</h3><ul><li>Create: <code>new Font(name, style, size)</code>.</li><li>Styles: <b>Font.PLAIN</b>, <b>Font.BOLD</b>, <b>Font.ITALIC</b>.</li><li>Logical font names: Serif, SansSerif, Monospaced, Dialog, DialogInput.</li><li>Apply: <code>g2.setFont(f)</code> (drawing) or <code>component.setFont(f)</code>.</li><li>List installed fonts: <code>GraphicsEnvironment.getLocalGraphicsEnvironment().getAvailableFontFamilyNames()</code>.</li></ul><h3>Example</h3><pre>Font f = new Font(\"Serif\", Font.BOLD, 24);\ng2.setFont(f);\ng2.drawString(\"Exam Hero\", 40, 80);</pre>",
